The Healthgrades website is geo-blocked in this environment — every URL I try (homepage, dentist search, zip search) returns HTTP 403 with the message "This page is not available in your area. Our servers have detected that you are accessing this site from a restricted area."

I cannot bypass a regional access restriction, and doing so would be inappropriate. This is not a sign-in/payment blocker (no such page was reached) — it's a hard region-based denial at the server level, so no dentist data is retrievable.

ANSWER: {"answer": "Blocked: Healthgrades returns HTTP 403 'This page is not available in your area' (region-restricted access) for the homepage and all search URLs attempted (e.g., /dentists/zip-90210, /search?what=dentist&where=90210). No sign-in, account, payment, or personal data was requested. Unable to retrieve any pediatric dentist near 90210 because the site denies access from this region."}
